{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfZniB3d2SMCdeCKu4QtH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written the repaired candidate, `glimpse_evidence_accumulation`, and it passes the self-check with `OK`. Novelty against the other models, full-fit convergence and the 30-minute speed limit are not covered by the self-check, so admission still has to decide those.\n\n**Why the first attempt was rejected.** It gave each person their own memory-window width. Averaged over people, that predicted almost exactly what `windowed_glimpse_expectation` predicts, so it was rejected as a near-duplicate.\n\n**What changed.** I still refine `windowed_glimpse_expectation`, but this time I change how people combine their glimpses. Before, the mismatch between what each glimpse shows and what the person expects was averaged across glimpses. Now it is added up. A longer sequence gives more glimpses, so it is judged more decisively than a short one with the same average mismatch. This follows the critique's second discrepancy: people's choices on short sequences follow alternation less than the incumbent predicts (0.116 observed vs 0.168 predicted). That one did not survive the FDR correction (q = 0.136).\n\n**Why it should pass the novelty check.** Adding up instead of averaging changes predictions across lengths 4–8, not just their overall scale. At the two-flip window, a length-8 sequence gives 7 glimpses and a length-4 sequence gives 3. So this version should differ from the parent model across the 512-pair novelty pool.\n\n**Self-check results:**\n- **ELPD-LOO:** finite, at -1022.7 on the short smoke fit. That is below the live models' roughly -1008, but it comes from only 100 draws on one chain.\n- **LOO reliability:** 6.5% of trials had high Pareto k, which the check reported as unreliable PSIS-LOO.\n- **R-hat:** unavailable, because the fit had a single chain.\n\nThe three files (`hypothesis.md`, `model_name.txt`, `candidate.py`) are in `experiment1/model_loop/iter_2/candidate_5_repair_1/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3439,"cache_read_input_tokens":62210,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3439,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"94440253-ac84-4300-b829-8f0efadcb44c","uuid":"d3e87796-6593-4366-b594-c1487b363a12","timestamp":"2026-09-30T14:34:01.233Z","request_id":"req_011CfZni9uf1Tv33EuEWddzy"}
